# Commit and push after a build

This applies to the iOS app (`ios/`) only. Firmware work (`firmware/`, `sim/`) is committed and pushed
only after the user has tested it on the watch and says it works.

After a build of the iOS app succeeds, commit the changes that build includes and push them to `origin`.

- Do this for device, simulator, and test builds that compile the current work.
- Write one or two sentences on why the change exists, matching recent commit style.
- Leave out secrets, `DerivedData`, and `xcuserdata`.
- Skip the commit when the build failed or there is nothing new to commit.
- Do not amend, and do not force-push.
